    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between 1891 and 1896, Sand Coulee produced 600,000 tons of bituminous coal that fueled Great Falls, Butte, East Helena smelters and Great Northern Railway engines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128359"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mines in Sand Coulee closed during the 1920s and 1930s as electricity and natural gas replaced coal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128359"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sand Coulee grew three distinct sections—Shacktown, Middletown (Finn Town), and Downtown—reflecting its mining heritage.",
